a supported ROCm serving runtime.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The campaign report exists and covers every model in the supported model\n  set, with a recorded functional pass/fail result per model.\n- The campaign report records performance parity measurements for each\n  functionally passing model against the CUDA serving baseline, using a\n  documented, reproducible measurement method.\n- The campaign report states an explicit go/no-go list of cleared models\n  that can be used to scope the productized ROCm serving runtime.\n- Each served model in the campaign was exercised through the same KServe\n  deployment surface (InferenceService/ServingRuntime) the platform uses in\n  production, and the deployment configuration used is captured in the\n  report.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of\n  the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Hardware access is unresolved and externally controlled: no AMD Instinct\n  nodes exist in the CI fleet, and procurement or partner-lab access timing\n  cannot be compressed by engineering work. This is an availability\n  precondition, not an acceptance criterion; the campaign starts once access\n  is secured.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image releases are controlled by AMD and the\n  upstream communities; the campaign should pin and record the exact image\n  versions used so results are reproducible.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32724,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a681020036e7f1","agent_id":"a2cf4b4145fd98259","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"49f5c511-64c8-41a1-a071-4051b86ff470","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:31:15.697Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 i