ning is documented in the release metadata.\n- A ServingRuntime packaging exists that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime, and\n  each model on the campaign's cleared list serves successfully through a\n  KServe InferenceService using that runtime on AMD GPU nodes.\n- The runtime is declared supported for exactly the cleared model list, and\n  models that failed the campaign are explicitly excluded from the supported\n  set.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities and may not align with platform release trains; the pinned,\n  validated-image approach above is the mitigation. If cadence misalignment\n  blocks consuming an upstream image for a target release, the build\n  approach is reworked against the nearest available validated upstream\n  build.\n- The go/no-go scope of this epic (which models are supported) is set by the\n  validation campaign's report; if no models clear, this epic's\n  productization scope is empty and the epic is removed.\n- KServe itself requires no code change for this capability: the runtime is\n  deployed through the existing ServingRuntime/InferenceService surfaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33560,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a681020036e7f1","agent_id":"a2cf4b4145fd98259","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"dc436df5-eea5-4a13-bdbd-10a673fde0e8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:31:28.529Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
