g work): PyTorch training\n  on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through\n  Kueue — this epic covers the Training Operator / PyTorchJob execution\n  side.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation requires physical AMD GPU nodes with a working ROCm driver\n  stack; node availability is an environment precondition shared with the\n  serving validation campaign.\n- PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled upstream; image versions\n  should be pinned to validated builds.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34380,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a681020036e7f1","agent_id":"a2cf4b4145fd98259","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"433fe2aa-e2a8-4968-9369-6ed9cff12e88","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:31:37.110Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
