es.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1, shared with the PyTorch ROCm training-support work): PyTorch\n  training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted\n  through Kueue, with `amd.com/gpu` quota handling — this epic covers the\n  Kueue quota/admission side.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation requires a cluster with AMD GPU nodes exposing the\n  `amd.com/gpu` resource (device plugin and node provisioning are cluster\n  infrastructure outside this strategy's components).\n- Configuration-level validation can largely proceed against the existing\n  quota model; only final admission validation needs live AMD GPU nodes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35043,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a681020036e7f1","agent_id":"a2cf4b4145fd98259","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"fd65ad69-c1ed-4903-a36f-f84fb7b50970","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:31:47.564Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
