rces on ROCm nodes.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n56\t  on AMD GPU nodes.\n57\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n58\t  on AMD GPU nodes with multi-GPU collectives functioning (verified by a\n59\t  distributed training run).\n60\t- PyTorchJobs requesting AMD GPU resources are admitted and run when Kueue\n61\t  workload queueing is enabled.\n62\t- The ROCm training images are built and released through the existing\n63\t  Training Operator image release flow.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared with the Kueue quota-handling work): PyTorch training\n68\t  on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through\n69\t  Kueue — this epic covers the Training Operator / PyTorchJob execution\n70\t  side.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Validation requires physical AMD GPU nodes with a working ROCm driver\n75\t  stack; node availability is an environment precondition shared with the\n76\t  serving validation campaign.\n77\t- PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled upstream; image versions\n78\t  should be pinned to validated builds.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf1e7979e9c1f7e","agent_id":"ac6b1845a0d7d2121","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"aa91247b-1856-45ab-8359-f7680831200d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:33.224Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94f614b0ae4b00e5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
