{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b77b3d008729c8f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for AMD GPUs (amd.com/gpu)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for AMD GPUs (amd.com/gpu)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes AMD GPUs a quota-managed resource in the platform's\n34\tqueueing layer, so that training jobs requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources\n35\tare admitted through Kueue with proper quota accounting — mirroring how\n36\tNVIDIA GPU quota is handled today. It covers the Kueue configuration\n37\tsurfaces (quota flavors and queues) and their validation for ROCm training\n38\tworkloads.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define Kueue quota configuration for `amd.com/gpu` resources\n43\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota flavors covering AMD GPU nodes).\n44\t- Validate that PyTorchJobs and other queueable workloads requesting\n45\t  `amd.com/gpu` are admitted, queued, and quota-accounted correctly,\n46\t  including all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics for multi-GPU jobs.\n47\t- Fix any Distributed Workloads stack changes needed for correct\n48\t  `amd.com/gpu` resource handling in admission and quota accounting.\n49\t- Expose queue-level visibility for AMD GPU workloads consistent with\n50\t  existing queueing metrics.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration exists that grants and accounts\n55\t  `amd.com/gpu` quota, and a job requesting `amd.com/gpu` within quota is\n56\t  admitted.\n57\t- A job requesting `amd.com/gpu` beyond its queue's quota is held pending\n58\t  (not partially admitted), demonstrating correct quota enforcement.\n59\t- A multi-GPU training job is admitted with all-or-nothing semantics —\n60\t  either all requested AMD GPUs are granted or the job waits.\n61\t- Admission and quota behavior for AMD GPU workloads is validated with\n62\t  queueing enabled on a cluster with AMD GPU nodes.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared with the PyTorch ROCm training-support work): PyTorch\n67\t  training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted\n68\t  through Kueue, with `amd.com/gpu` quota handling — this epic covers the\n69\t  Kueue quota/admission side.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- Validation requires a cluster with AMD GPU nodes exposing the\n74\t  `amd.com/gpu` resource (device plugin and node provisioning are cluster\n75\t  infrastructure outside this strategy's components).\n76\t- Configuration-level validation can largely proceed against the existing\n77\t  quota model; only final admission validation needs live AMD GPU nodes.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf1e7979e9c1f7e","agent_id":"ac6b1845a0d7d2121","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"7d05036e-29c3-4ca9-8821-75ea0f5e2fbf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:34.091Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b77b3d008729c8f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
