raining workloads.\n52\t  - Installing and using the ROCm serving runtime through the platform's\n53\t    serving stack.\n54\t- Content is authored through the Red Hat docs content process and\n55\t  technically reviewed against the implemented and validated behavior.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware and the driver\n60\t  prerequisites for both serving and training on ROCm.\n61\t- Published documentation states the validated model list, matching the\n62\t  go/no-go scope established by the validation campaign and the supported\n63\t  set of the productized runtime.\n64\t- Published documentation covers quota configuration for AMD GPU training\n65\t  workloads admitted through Kueue.\n66\t- All new content is technically reviewed against the implemented\n67\t  behavior by engineers from the implementing teams, with review sign-off\n68\t  recorded.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n73\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- Content depends on the outcomes of the validation campaign and the\n78\t  implementation work; authoring cannot complete before those deliverables\n79\t  exist.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf1e7979e9c1f7e","agent_id":"ac6b1845a0d7d2121","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"68bd869b-2f51-422b-9589-be5fb130e9c3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:34.787Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-959ad60fc68eb57e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
