{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bf373d8b6316f8a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears only part of the model set, the productized\n15\t    runtime's supported-model scope shrinks to the cleared list; if no models clear\n16\t    parity, productization does not proceed and the epic is removed.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for\n39\tthe models cleared by the AMD Instinct validation campaign. Today only CUDA\n40\t(NVIDIA) runtime builds are productized; ROCm builds exist upstream but are\n41\tneither shipped nor supported. The epic turns the campaign's go/no-go scope\n42\tinto a shippable runtime: midstream builds of the vLLM ROCm runtime,\n43\tpackaging as a ServingRuntime for the platform, and validation that the\n44\truntime serves the cleared models under KServe on AMD Instinct nodes.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add ROCm build variants of the vLLM serving runtime to the existing\n49\t  midstream productization flow (the same flow that ships the CUDA builds).\n50\t- Pin the upstream ROCm runtime image/base versions the builds are cut from,\n51\t  recording the exact validated digests.\n52\t- Define and ship the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime packaging that\n53\t  deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime on AMD GPU nodes for the cleared model set.\n54\t- Validate serving of each cleared model through the packaged runtime under\n55\t  KServe InferenceServices on AMD Instinct hardware (both the functional\n56\t  result and the deployment surface used in the campaign).\n57\t- Ensure the new runtime image builds and passes the existing build pipeline\n58\t  used for serving runtime releases.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image is built in the midstream productization\n63\t  flow and passes the existing build pipeline (pipeline green on the ROCm\n64\t  variant).\n65\t- The shipped runtime pins a recorded, validated ROCm image/base version,\n66\t  and the pinning is documented in the release metadata.\n67\t- A ServingRuntime packaging exists that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime, and\n68\t  each model on the campaign's cleared list serves successfully through a\n69\t  KServe InferenceService using that runtime on AMD GPU nodes.\n70\t- The runtime is declared supported for exactly the cleared model list, and\n71\t  models that failed the campaign are explicitly excluded from the supported\n72\t  set.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n77\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n78\t\n79\t## Risks / Notes\n80\t\n81\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n82\t  communities and may not align with platform release trains; the pinned,\n83\t  validated-image approach above is the mitigation. If cadence misalignment\n84\t  blocks consuming an upstream image for a target release, the build\n85\t  approach is reworked against the nearest available validated upstream\n86\t  build.\n87\t- The go/no-go scope of this epic (which models are supported) is set by the\n88\t  validation campaign's report; if no models clear, this epic's\n89\t  productization scope is empty and the epic is removed.\n90\t- KServe itself requires no code change for this capability: the runtime is\n91\t  deployed through the existing ServingRuntime/InferenceService surfaces.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a829e20fcd2861","agent_id":"a0fbfd4fec95aca89","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"028d0fcc-ccec-412e-a19c-597e7a9c4bfa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:38:47.896Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bf373d8b6316f8a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
