{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ac00040f1fa81ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support through the Training Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support through the Training Operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables PyTorch training on ROCm for single- and multi-GPU jobs\n34\texecuted as PyTorchJobs through the Training Operator. It covers\n35\tROCm-capable training images and the job-level support needed for\n36\tmulti-GPU (ROCm collective communication) execution, so that distributed\n37\ttraining workloads run on AMD GPU nodes the same way CUDA-based PyTorchJobs\n38\trun today.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Provide ROCm-capable PyTorch training images for job execution through\n43\t  the Training Operator, including multi-GPU collective communication\n44\t  support appropriate to ROCm.\n45\t- Validate single-GPU PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes with ROCm\n46\t  images.\n47\t- Validate multi-GPU (and, where job topologies require, multi-node)\n48\t  PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes, including gang-scheduled\n49\t  admission through Kueue when workload queueing is enabled.\n50\t- Fix any Training Operator changes needed for job pods requesting AMD GPU\n51\t  resources on ROCm nodes.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n56\t  on AMD GPU nodes.\n57\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n58\t  on AMD GPU nodes with multi-GPU collectives functioning (verified by a\n59\t  distributed training run).\n60\t- PyTorchJobs requesting AMD GPU resources are admitted and run when Kueue\n61\t  workload queueing is enabled.\n62\t- The ROCm training images are built and released through the existing\n63\t  Training Operator image release flow.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared with the Kueue quota-handling work): PyTorch training\n68\t  on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through\n69\t  Kueue — this epic covers the Training Operator / PyTorchJob execution\n70\t  side.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Validation requires physical AMD GPU nodes with a working ROCm driver\n75\t  stack; node availability is an environment precondition shared with the\n76\t  serving validation campaign.\n77\t- PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled upstream; image versions\n78\t  should be pinned to validated builds.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a829e20fcd2861","agent_id":"a0fbfd4fec95aca89","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"2cacbb4d-2c20-448b-87be-237309df285f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:38:48.915Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ac00040f1fa81ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
