{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98cbccc7ef758a54","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: 'AMD Instinct validation campaign: vLLM ROCm functional and performance parity'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign: vLLM ROCm functional and performance parity\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on\n30\tAMD Instinct accelerators reaches functional and performance parity with the\n31\tproductized CUDA builds for the platform's supported model set. It runs a\n32\tvalidation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware using upstream ROCm\n33\tbuilds of vLLM and produces the go/no-go scope that determines which models\n34\tthe productized ROCm serving runtime must support. The deliverable is a\n35\tvalidated campaign report with per-model functional results, performance\n36\tparity data against the CUDA baseline, and an explicit cleared/failed model\n37\tlist.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n42\t  access — see Risks; the access itself is an externally-controlled\n43\t  precondition, while standing up the validation environment on secured\n44\t  hardware is in scope here).\n45\t- Stand up the validation environment on the secured hardware: AMD GPU\n46\t  driver stack, ROCm runtime, and upstream vLLM ROCm serving images.\n47\t- Define the campaign protocol for the supported model set: per-model\n48\t  functional pass/fail criteria and performance parity measurements against\n49\t  the CUDA serving baseline.\n50\t- Execute the campaign: serve each supported model via vLLM on ROCm under\n51\t  the KServe deployment surfaces used by the platform, collecting functional\n52\t  and performance data.\n53\t- Produce the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance\n54\t  parity data, and the go/no-go cleared model list that scopes productization\n55\t  of a supported ROCm serving runtime.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The campaign report exists and covers every model in the supported model\n60\t  set, with a recorded functional pass/fail result per model.\n61\t- The campaign report records performance parity measurements for each\n62\t  functionally passing model against the CUDA serving baseline, using a\n63\t  documented, reproducible measurement method.\n64\t- The campaign report states an explicit go/no-go list of cleared models\n65\t  that can be used to scope the productized ROCm serving runtime.\n66\t- Each served model in the campaign was exercised through the same KServe\n67\t  deployment surface (InferenceService/ServingRuntime) the platform uses in\n68\t  production, and the deployment configuration used is captured in the\n69\t  report.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n74\t  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of\n75\t  the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Hardware access is unresolved and externally controlled: no AMD Instinct\n80\t  nodes exist in the CI fleet, and procurement or partner-lab access timing\n81\t  cannot be compressed by engineering work. This is an availability\n82\t  precondition, not an acceptance criterion; the campaign starts once access\n83\t  is secured.\n84\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image releases are controlled by AMD and the\n85\t  upstream communities; the campaign should pin and record the exact image\n86\t  versions used so results are reproducible.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae49ff7a34a034a3","agent_id":"a15de2d1f4fd63bdd","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"4336d161-54d0-4fc2-a400-1ed990403b9f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:40:57.315Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98cbccc7ef758a54","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
