{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-803ecb0d93abdd19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support through the Training Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support through the Training Operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables PyTorch training on ROCm for single- and multi-GPU jobs\n34\texecuted as PyTorchJobs through the Training Operator. It covers\n35\tROCm-capable training images and the job-level support needed for\n36\tmulti-GPU (ROCm collective communication) execution, so that distributed\n37\ttraining workloads run on AMD GPU nodes the same way CUDA-based PyTorchJobs\n38\trun today.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Provide ROCm-capable PyTorch training images for job execution through\n43\t  the Training Operator, including multi-GPU collective communication\n44\t  support appropriate to ROCm.\n45\t- Validate single-GPU PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes with ROCm\n46\t  images.\n47\t- Validate multi-GPU (and, where job topologies require, multi-node)\n48\t  PyTorchJob execution on AMD GPU nodes, including gang-scheduled\n49\t  admission through Kueue when workload queueing is enabled.\n50\t- Fix any Training Operator changes needed for job pods requesting AMD GPU\n51\t  resources on ROCm nodes.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n56\t  on AMD GPU nodes.\n57\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm training image completes successfully\n58\t  on AMD GPU nodes with multi-GPU collectives functioning (verified by a\n59\t  distributed training run).\n60\t- PyTorchJobs requesting AMD GPU resources are admitted and run when Kueue\n61\t  workload queueing is enabled. This epic's validation responsibility for\n62\t  that admission surface is job runnability under queueing (the job, once\n63\t  admitted, actually runs on AMD GPU nodes); `amd.com/gpu` quota accounting\n64\t  and enforcement are validated by the Kueue quota-handling work, not here.\n65\t- The ROCm training images are built and released through the existing\n66\t  Training Operator image release flow.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared with the Kueue quota-handling work): PyTorch training\n71\t  on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through\n72\t  Kueue — this epic covers the Training Operator / PyTorchJob execution\n73\t  side, with validation responsibility for job runnability under queueing;\n74\t  quota accounting and enforcement for `amd.com/gpu` belong to the Kueue\n75\t  quota-handling work.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Validation requires physical AMD GPU nodes with a working ROCm driver\n80\t  stack; node availability is an environment precondition shared with the\n81\t  serving validation campaign.\n82\t- PyTorch ROCm image releases are controlled upstream; image versions\n83\t  should be pinned to validated builds.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae49ff7a34a034a3","agent_id":"a15de2d1f4fd63bdd","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"a9c913fe-00f2-4807-8c56-ceb27f9b6fb2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:40:58.947Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-803ecb0d93abdd19","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
