alidated model list.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- New documentation topics covering:\n53\t  - Supported AMD hardware (Instinct accelerators) for serving and training.\n54\t  - Driver and ROCm runtime prerequisites for AMD GPU nodes.\n55\t  - The validated model list for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime, including\n56\t    explicitly unsupported (failed-parity) models where relevant.\n57\t  - Configuring Kueue quota for `amd.com/gpu` training workloads.\n58\t  - Installing and using the ROCm serving runtime through the platform's\n59\t    serving stack.\n60\t- Content is authored through the Red Hat docs content process and\n61\t  technically reviewed against the implemented and validated behavior.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware and the driver\n66\t  prerequisites for both serving and training on ROCm.\n67\t- Published documentation states the validated model list, matching the\n68\t  go/no-go scope established by the validation campaign and the supported\n69\t  set of the productized runtime.\n70\t- Published documentation covers quota configuration for AMD GPU training\n71\t  workloads admitted through Kueue.\n72\t- All new content is technically reviewed against the implemented\n73\t  behavior by engineers from the implementing teams, with review sign-off\n74\t  recorded.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n79\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks / Notes\n82\t\n83\t- Content depends on the outcomes of the validation campaign and the\n84\t  implementation work; authoring cannot complete before those deliverables\n85\t  exist.\n86\t- This epic is gated on the validation campaign: if no models clear the\n87\t  parity bar (and the serving-runtime productization work is removed\n88\t  accordingly), the productized-runtime usage topic is replaced by\n89\t  documentation of the failed-parity outcome and an explicitly unsupported\n90\t  model list; the hardware, driver, and quota topics stand as written.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae49ff7a34a034a3","agent_id":"a15de2d1f4fd63bdd","session_id":"3c5f0377-4b7e-4251-9827-8f66cc239d73","uuid":"989ed3c5-5ec5-46d3-80e4-b2abc70e4830","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:41:00.315Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a177b41df58de5f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
